{
  "_about": "Skill-tree grid positions read off in-game screenshots the user supplied, in skills/. Each entry gives the cell a skill occupies on the 3-wide, 6-tall tree grid, which is what SkillDesc.txt's SkillRow/SkillColumn encode. Matching by coordinate rather than by list order is what makes a name pairing possible: the two sources disagree on order but agree on position.",
  "_provenance": "Read from the screenshots in skills/ by a subagent using read_image plus magnified crops of every panel and label, and with programmatic detection of the white name-label boxes to pin the grid columns. Names transcribed exactly as shown.",
  "_whyThisMatters": "An earlier attempt paired English with the 易牙居 list by assuming the grid is read row-major. That agreed on some trees and drifted on others (the Amazon bow tree matched six of ten, the Sorceress lightning tree swapped two). The screenshots show the grid reading is not the issue at all - the cell coordinate is.",
  "_clientNotes": {
    "classScreenshots": "亞馬遜, 刺客, 野蠻人, 德魯伊, 死靈法師, 聖騎士 - Traditional Chinese, classic TW client, each showing all three trees side by side.",
    "sorceress": "The three 法師*.jpg are a different window (tabs 冰系法术 / 雷系法术 / 火系法术, footer 0 技能点 剩余) and their names are Simplified. Their cell coordinates are still usable, but they come from a different client build, so the Sorceress layout is the one tree set not confirmed against a Traditional screenshot.",
    "emptyFirstCell": "Trees that leave row 1 column 1 empty: Amazon bow, all three Assassin trees, Barbarian combat, Druid summoning, Necromancer poison-and-bone and curses, and all three Sorceress trees. This matches SkillDesc.txt, where e.g. Magic Arrow and Fire Bolt both sit at row 1 column 2.",
    "uiMarker": "Every tree has exactly one dark circle-with-slash slot marker in an empty cell. It is a UI element, not a skill, and is not listed here."
  },
  "_unreadable": [
    "亞馬遜 bow tree row 5 column 2: the icon has no rendered name label in the screenshot. 易牙居's list has 砲轟 in this tree, which is Strafe, which is what SkillDesc.txt puts at row 5 column 2 - so the cell is identified even though the label is not legible."
  ],
  "_glyphVariants": [
    "火燄 vs 焰: the screenshots render 火焰箭, 火焰復甦 and 火焰石魔 with 焰. A first pass read these as the dense variant 燄; the user confirmed 焰, so 焰 is used throughout and 燄 appears nowhere.",
    "The Assassin last trap is 刀刃之盾; its first character is visually ambiguous between 刀 and 刃 at screenshot size. The user confirmed the set of spellings and did not flag this one, so it stands as read.",
    "User-confirmed forms: 黏土石魔 (not 黏土石模), 尋找藥劑 (not 葯), 抵抗閃電, 支配火焰 (not 燄), 武器格檔 (not 格擋), 旋風 (not 炫風), 戳刺 (the user first read this as 搓刺 and then confirmed 戳刺 is right), 鎌鼬風."
  ],
